## Web Application

This section introduces a generic web application architecture built using AWS infrastructure components.

The architecture includes:

- **EC2 Instances:** Host and run the web application.
- **S3 Bucket:** Provides object storage for application assets and files.
- **RDS Instance:** Provides managed relational database services.
- **Load Balancer:** Distributes incoming application traffic across EC2 instances.
- **Route 53:** Provides DNS management and domain name resolution.

This example introduces the fundamental AWS infrastructure components required to deploy a web application. The architecture will be refined and improved in later modules.

